---
import JasiLabLayout from "../../layouts/JasiLabLayout.astro";
---

<JasiLabLayout
  title="Delete your Tambla UG account - JasiLab"
  description="Request deletion of your Tambla UG account and associated personal data from CVT."
>
  <section class="section-band max-w-3xl">
    <p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-primary-deep">Tambla UG</p>
    <h1 class="display-lg mt-2">Request account deletion</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body leading-relaxed">
      Tambla UG is a product of
      <strong class="text-ink-strong">Connected Verification Digital Uganda Limited</strong> (trading as
      <strong class="text-ink-strong">CVT</strong>). You can request deletion of your Tambla account and associated
      personal data using the steps below.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-body leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink-strong">How to request deletion</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-3 pl-5">
        <li>
          Email
          <a href="mailto:privacy@cvt.ug?subject=Tambla%20UG%20account%20deletion%20request" class="text-primary-deep hover:text-primary"
            >privacy@cvt.ug</a
          >
          from a reachable address, or message WhatsApp support if you were given a support number.
        </li>
        <li>
          Use subject line: <strong class="text-ink-strong">Tambla UG account deletion request</strong>
        </li>
        <li>
          Include:
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>Your Tambla / WhatsApp phone number (with country code, e.g. +256…)</li>
            <li>Your full name as registered</li>
            <li>Optional: plate number or CVT verification ID if you have one</li>
            <li>A clear statement that you want your Tambla account and associated data deleted</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>We will verify it is you (for example by confirming an OTP or matching registration details).</li>
      </ol>

      <p>
        <a
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-primary-deep px-4 py-2 font-medium text-white hover:bg-primary"
          href="mailto:privacy@cvt.ug?subject=Tambla%20UG%20account%20deletion%20request&body=I%20request%20deletion%20of%20my%20Tambla%20UG%20account%20and%20associated%20data.%0A%0APhone%20(E.164)%3A%20%0AFull%20name%3A%20%0APlate%20(optional)%3A%20%0ACVT%20ID%20(optional)%3A%20%0A"
        >
          Email deletion request
        </a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink-strong">What we delete or retain</h2>
      <p>When your request is verified, we will delete or anonymise Tambla account data where the law allows, including:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li>Sign-in / session data tied to your Tambla account</li>
        <li>App profile details used only for Tambla membership where no longer required</li>
        <li>Device push tokens registered for your account</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Some records may be retained for a limited period where required for verification accountability, fraud
        prevention, disputes, security, or legal obligations (for example moderated trust / audit records under CVT’s
        retention schedule). We will not keep your account active for normal Tambla use after deletion is completed.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink-strong">How long it takes</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to complete verified deletion requests within <strong class="text-ink-strong">30 days</strong>. Complex
        cases (for example open disputes) may take longer; we will tell you if so.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink-strong">Related links</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li>
          <a href="/tambla/privacy" class="text-primary-deep hover:text-primary">Tambla UG Privacy Policy</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.cvt.co.ug/en/support/privacy" class="text-primary-deep hover:text-primary"
            >CVT platform Privacy Policy</a
          >
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</JasiLabLayout>
